"en-US" dirty="0" err="1"/><a:t>kΩ</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t> test resistors provided in hardware kit P/N 7300013 on TB3, TB4, and TB5. See Figure 4. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="457200" indent="-457200"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="170000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:buFont typeface="+mj-lt"/><a:buAutoNum type="arabicPeriod"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Configure the DIP switches as required. See Table 2, Table 3, Table 4, and Table 5. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="457200" indent="-457200"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="170000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:buFont typeface="+mj-lt"/><a:buAutoNum type="arabicPeriod"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Mount the SIGA-REL in the enclosure. Use the four #6 self-tapping screws and the four #6 flat washers provided in hardware kit P/N 235493. Figure 3 shows the typical mounting in an MFC-A cabinet. Use the provided drill template (P/N 260591) when mounting the SIGA-REL inside enclosures that do not provide predetermined mounting holes. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="457200" indent="-457200"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="170000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="600"/></a:spcBef><a:buFont typeface="+mj-lt"/><a:buAutoNum type="arabicPeriod"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Connect the field wires. Do not connect the releasing device circuits until after you have thoroughly tested the device. </a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree><p:extLst><p:ext uri="{BB962C8B-B14F-4D97-AF65-F5344CB8AC3E}"><p14:creationId xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" val="2159052057"/></p:ext></p:extLst></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>